---
// <BcnPlanItemsTable> — the plan's items as a sheet you can edit (2026-10-28, the SOW review: "edit records in a table
// view rather than row by row"), beside the Gantt on the Schedule tab (Show As: Chart or Table). Name, Level, Start,
// End, Date Type, Milestone, Owners, Status (Live) and Notes, one row per item in outline order.
//
// It is the budget sheet's spreadsheet (2026-10-30, Andy: "I really like the budget table, and hate how the Schedule
// table makes me click into a status cell, and then it transforms into a dropdown"): <BcnSheet>'s name box and value
// bar, cursor, keys and cell kinds. Its key: Editable (your draft's fields), Saves to Live (Status), Read-Only (a
// parent's dates, the level). The runtime is ./plan-items-table.ts.
//
// bcn-lego-checked: the table IS <BcnSheet> (AG Grid community on the spoke's Beacon theme, as the budget sheet and
// Beacon's grids are), its one-click pickers the sheet's. No esa- lego is an editable grid. No CSS of its own.
import BcnSheet from './BcnSheet.astro';
---

<BcnSheet class="bcn-pit" hooks="pit" data-bcn-plan-items-table>
  <Fragment slot="legend">
    <span data-legend="edit"><i></i>Editable</span>
    <span data-legend="live"><i></i>Saves to Live</span>
    <span data-legend="read"><i></i>Read-Only</span>
  </Fragment>
</BcnSheet>
